/meta.json` shows rowCount=2559, sourceFiles=24. FAILIF: any claim that the ingest rows caused the hang, or a substrate rewrite used as the fix.\nAC4 `python3 scripts/recall_battery.py` (AUG-176 worktree) runs to completion and writes per-project hit rates (target block in top-5) into evidence/AUG-176/06-recall-battery.md; every below-hit query carries a chunking/granularity fix or a named residual cause. PROOF: the committed report with a numeric hit rate per project. FAILIF: a missing report or asserted counts without the query list.\nAC5 NO FABRICATED EVIDENCE: probe transcripts are committed under evidence/AUG-178/, and registered/regenerable counts are read back by prefix (`GET /api/memories?namespace=auger&prefix=/auger/AUG176-code-factory/&limit=1000` -> 160 keys) and by `total` (2336 before, 2559 indexed), never asserted from a registration log alone. FAILIF: a count with no read-back command.","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-16T11:40:47.068852+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T06:44:48.315936+00:00","foreman_note":"AUG-178 — measured root cause, correcting this row's premise. Driver tick 2026-11-17T04:14-04:47Z.\n\nMEASURED: the hang was NOT caused by AUG-176's oversized ingest rows. Live namespace root is\n/home/kara/duckbrain/namespaces (NOT ~/.duckbrain-live, a stale copy — the earlier probe measured\nthe copy). auger's dir held a 0-byte `.search.rebuild.lock` (mtime 2026-11-01 03:28:45) and a\n`.search/` containing only `fts.duckdb.tmp` + `rows.tmp.jsonl` from 2026-10-30 — no sidecar, ever.\nEngine code src/search/index.ts:tryAcquireRebuildLock() steals only when\n`ageMs > STALE && pid !== null && !pidAlive(pid)`; an EMPTY lock parses to pid === null, so it is\nNEVER stolen → rebuildNamespaceIndex() waits for a lock that never vanishes → every ?q= and\n?contains= request hangs (client rc=124) while prefix reads stay fast (17-157 ms).\n\nFIX APPLIED (reversible housekeeping, auger only): the stale lock was moved to\n~/.hermes/goals/auger-stale-locks/a