 {"status":"pending","id":"AUG-180","title":"SUBSTRATE (duckbrain-owned): pid-less search-rebuild locks permanently block DuckBrain keyword search in 17 namespaces; auto-build bound counts lines not rows","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"072128dc31b670245cd31778d806063eed907c64b97eadae8474bb8408d3e024"},"priority":"P1","source":null,"reasoning":"Fleet-wide DuckBrain substrate defect measured 2026-11-17T04:14-04:47Z while resolving AUG-178.\n\n1) PID-LESS LOCKS ARE NEVER STOLEN. src/search/index.ts:tryAcquireRebuildLock() steals a lock only when `ageMs > REBUILD_LOCK_STALE_MS && pid !== null && !pidAlive(pid)`. A lock file with EMPTY content parses to pid === null, so it is never stolen at any age. rebuildNamespaceIndex() then waits for that lock to vanish → every ?q= and ?contains= request on the namespace hangs until the client times out (measured rc=124 at 40-120s on auger, crier, eduos), while prefix reads stay fast (17-157 ms) because they never touch the sidecar.\n2) ONE BULK SWEEP CREATED SUCH LOCKS. Census of the live root /home/kara/duckbrain/namespaces (318 namespaces): 249 have a usable sidecar (fts.duckdb), 68 carry a pid-less 0-byte .search.rebuild.lock with mtime 2026-11-01 03:28:45-47, and 17 of those have NO sidecar → keyword/hybrid search on them is dead today: ai-plays-poke, apocalyptic, asce, auger, auger-aug114-gridless, auger-aug114-repro, auger-nasa-demo-2114906, boardctl, code-factory, coding-hermes-tools, crier, df18, eduos, eduos.dexdat.com.co, gr2-probe-1793214725, project, terminal-jail-review.\n   auger was repaired this fire by moving its stale lock aside (sidecar rebuilt in 15.6s, rowCount=2559) — evidence/auger evidence/AUG-178/).\n3) THE AUTO-BUILD BOUND COUNTS LINES, NOT ROWS. countSourceRowsUpTo() counts 0x0a bytes across every *.jsonl and compares to DUCKBRAIN_SEARCH_AUTOBUILD_MAX_ROWS (5000). Namespace cos has 63 memories but 36,062 source lines across 43 files, so it refuses keyword search with HTTP 500 \"auto-build skipped: namespace 'cos' has more than 5000 source rows\" — every namespace whose store files exceed 5000 lines can never self-heal its sidecar from a read path, and multi-line content (or history) makes that trivially true.\n\nConsequence: fleet recall (foreman Step 3 recall, auger recall, any ?q=/contains= client) is degraded or dead on the 17 namespaces and permanently un-self-healing on any >5000-line namespace; the AUG-176 AC3 recall battery was blocked by it and is now runnable on auger.\n\nOWNERSHIP: the substrate is duckbrain-owned (/home/kara/duckbrain). This row is filed on the auger board because it blocks auger work; the fix must land in the duckbrain repo and be routed to that lane.","review_notes":null,"ts":null,"acceptance_criteria":"AC1 CENSUS ZERO: `for d in /home/kara/duckbrain/namespaces/*/; do [ -f \"$d/.search.rebuild.lock\" ] && ! grep -q '\"pid\"' \"$d/.search.rebuild.lock\" 2>/dev/null && [ ! -f \"$d/.search/fts.duckdb\" ] && basename $d; done` expects EMPTY output (measured pre-fix: 17 namespaces). FAILIF: any name printed.\nAC2 CODE FIX: `grep -n \"pid !== null\" /home/kara/duckbrain/src/search/index.ts` expects NO match (the steal condition must treat a missing pid as stale once the lock is aged), and a test in the duckbrain suite asserts that an EMPTY lock older than REBUILD_LOCK_STALE_MS is stolen and the rebuild completes. PROOF: the test name plus its pass count. FAILIF: the old conjunct is still present.\nAC3 BOUND IS ROWS, NOT LINES: `timeout 60 curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code} %{time_total}' -H \"x-api-key: <token>\" \"http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/memories?namespace=cos&contains=recall&limit=3\"` expects `200` (pre-fix: 500 \"auto-build skipped: namespace 'cos' has more than 5000 source rows\" for a 63-memory namespace). FAILIF: the same 500, or any refusal whose cause is a line count rather than a memory-row count.\nAC4 SWEEP WITH READ-BACK: each of the 17 namespaces listed in the row's reasoning answers one bounded `?contains=` probe with `200` within 30s, and for each the sweep records `cat <ns>/.search/meta.json` (rowCount/sourceFiles). PROOF: a committed transcript listing namespace, http_code, time_total, rowCount. FAILIF: any rc=124, any missing sidecar afterwards, or a count asserted without the meta read-back.\nAC5 OWNERSHIP AND ROUTING: the fix lands in the duckbrain repo with its own commit hash referenced here, and the row records the duckbrain lane/board that owns it — no auger code change is presented as the fix, and no substrate content is rewritten. FAILIF: an auger-side workaround claimed as the fix.\nAC6 NO SIDE EFFECT ON LIVE READS: after the sweep, `GET /api/memories?namespace=auger&limit=1` still answers 200 with total unchanged (>=2559) and prefix reads stay under 200ms. FAILIF: a read regression or a dropped-row count.\n\nCONTEXT: auger itself was unblocked 2026-11-17 by moving its pid-less lock aside (evidence/AUG-178/02-root-cause-lock.txt); this row is the durable, fleet-wide fix and belongs to the duckbrain repo/lane.","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-17T04:34:31Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T04:34:31Z","foreman_note":null,"capability_tags":[],"depends_on":[],"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worktree":null,"branch":null,"sessions":null,"type":"bug","initiative_refs":["auger:docs/qa/aug176-conversion-coverage.md#recall"]}
 {"status":"pending","id":"AUG-181","title":"Recall registration is not idempotent: every corpus key is stored twice in the auger namespace and duplicate rows consume the retrieval window","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"9b4bb6bad3c16b264524267988a533bf662bcd4ac1af22e4b350dec236723329"},"priority":"P2","source":null,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-17 while closing AUG-178 AC4: register was run twice on 2026-11-16 (the second a retry after a 500 on CHD-NORMATIVE-MANIFEST-PREAMBLE-S000-P01) and a memory write APPENDS, so every /auger/AUG176-*/<BLOCK-ID> key resolves to 2 rows. The battery's 'top-5' was therefore a top-2..4 distinct-block measurement (8/12 and 5/12) until the battery itself de-duplicated (11/12 and 9/12 on the same tree). DuckBrain has no DELETE route for a memory row, so the duplication is permanent per prefix and every future register run doubles it again.","review_notes":null,"ts":null,"acceptance_criteria":"NON-IDEMPOTENT REGISTRATION: `scripts/recall_battery.py register` appends a new memory row every time it runs, and DuckBrain exposes no DELETE route for a memory row, so the `auger` namespace now stores EVERY `/auger/AUG176-*/<BLOCK-ID>` key at least TWICE (measured 2026-11-17: 2 rows for every sampled key). Because the retrieval surface returns one row per stored row, duplicate rows consume the candidate window: the recall battery's \"top-5\" was really \"top-2..4 distinct blocks\" until the battery itself was fixed to de-duplicate (AUG-176/AUG-178). Ranking quality therefore depends on how many times the corpus was registered, which is not something the corpus should encode.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: any future `register` run (a re-chunk, a corpus refresh, a repaired manifest) doubles the namespace again and dilutes every query's window further; there is no cleanup path through the API, so the damage is permanent per prefix.\n\nAC1 DUPLICATE CENSUS BY READ-BACK: a new `python3 scripts/recall_battery.py census` (or an equivalent documented command) prints, per project, `keys`, `rows`, and `duplicate_keys`, sampled over the whole prefix; expect the numbers to be derived from `GET /api/memories?namespace=auger&prefix=<key>&limit=100` counts and not from a registration log. PROOF: the command's own output committed under evidence/AUG-176/. FAILIF: a count with no read-back command, or a census that samples fewer than 20 keys per project.\n\nAC2 IDEMPOTENT REGISTER: running `register` twice in a row on an already-registered, unchanged corpus writes ZERO new rows the second time — expect the second run to print `rows_written=0` (with `skipped_existing` naming how many keys were already present), and a read-back of any key to still show exactly ONE row for keys registered after the fix. FAILIF: a second run that writes rows, or a post-fix key with more than one row.\n\nAC3 NO LOSS IN THE FIX: every block id of the three corpora still resolves after the change — expect `spec validate` rc 0 on all three corpora, and the recall battery re-run to report per-project hit rates that are NOT lower than the 2026-11-17 baseline (code-factory 11/12, auger-docs 9/12, coding-hermes-director 7/12, total 27/36). PROOF: the three numbers in the committed report. FAILIF: a missing block, or a hit rate below baseline with no cause named.\n\nAC4 HONEST DECISION RECORDED: the row records which path was taken, and the choice is one of (a) register into a FRESH prefix (e.g. `/auger/AUG176b/<BLOCK-ID>`) and point the battery at it, or (b) a substrate-side action that removes duplicate rows, which is duckbrain-owned and must be routed (AUG-180) rather than faked with an allowlist. Expect the row's note to name the prefix the battery reads and the reason the other path was not taken. FAILIF: a fix that rewrites the substrate content, or a battery that quietly tolerates duplicates.\n\nCONTEXT: measured while closing AUG-178 AC4 / AUG-176 AC3 (evidence/AUG-176/06-recall-battery.md, red-proof evidence/AUG-176/07-battery-red-proof.txt). The battery-side de-duplication is already committed; this row is the durable registration-side fix.","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-17T06:45:07Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T06:45:07Z","foreman_note":null,"capability_tags":[],"depends_on":[],"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worktree":null,"branch":null,"sessions":null,"type":"bug","initiative":"auger-endstate"}
